By Le Chatelier's principle:

- remove the liquid phosgene through the tap and keep it condensed below 8 °C, so the gases continue reacting;
- use high pressure (2 mol of gas form 0 mol of gas), favouring the products;
- keep feeding in CO and Cl$_2$;
- keep the vessel cool (exothermic). In practice a moderate temperature with a catalyst is a compromise with rate.
